{"episodes":{"159517":"During the late evening of Thursday, August 5th, a cluster of thunderstorms developed across the eastern Twin Cities metro area and produced isolated hail reports from Woodbury, southward to Cottage Grove. Most of the hail was sub-severe but a couple of reports of quarter size hail were noted. A severe downburst also occurred late Thursday evening as a large tree was blown down along with a pontoon boat flipped.","159717":"A midlevel shortwave trough trekked across the region. This feature tapped into residual moisture to produce scattered showers and thunderstorms. The stronger storms produced gusty winds in excess of 58 mph across portions of western Colorado.","159740":"Several strong thunderstorms affected the nearshore and shore areas of Lake Michigan from Sheboygan south to Kenosha during the late afternoon on August 6th.","160304":"Several severe thunderstorms impacted portions of southern Wisconsin, especially near Lake Michigan as storms developed across central Wisconsin and eventually morphed into a line that dropped south into Illinois.","160836":"A thunderstorm formed in the lee of the Wind River Range and become severe as it crossed the Wind River Basin. A former NWS employee reported quarter-sized hail near Ethete. At Central Wyoming Regional Airport, a maximum wind gust of 60 mph was recorded.","160917":"A thunderstorm briefly became severe over northeastern Crook County, producing quarter sized hail near Colony.","160918":"A thunderstorm briefly became severe over the central Black Hills, producing a few wind gusts to 70 mph near Pactola Reservoir.","160919":"A cluster of severe thunderstorms tracked across far southwestern into south central South Dakota during the late afternoon and early evening hours. The storms produced small hail and wind gusts of 60 to 70 mph across portions of the area.","160924":"Lightning struck a moviegoer at an east metro drive-in theater as storms moved through the area. The man was hit about 10:25 p.m at the Vali-Hi Drive-In on just north of Interstate 94 in Lake Elmo.","161057":"Scattered thunderstorms moved across portions of northwest Indiana during the afternoon of August 6th.","161284":"An isolated thunderstorm produced some severe wind gusts around Park County.","161301":"Scattered thunderstorms moved through the region on the 6th of August producing strong wind gusts including an observed 77 MPH gust near Laramie. Additional storms throughout the afternoon and evening produced wind gusts around 55 MPH.","161920":"Widespread severe weather occurred in southeast Idaho.","162218":"An MCV moved across the area during afternoon peak heating. Isolated severe storms with downburst winds, hail, and localized flooding.","162219":"An mesoscale convective vortex moved across the area during afternoon peak heating. Thunderstorms developed and produced occasional downburst winds, hail, and localized flooding.","162245":"Scattered thunderstorms developed and moved slowly west across southeast Arizona. Large hail was reported near Rio Rico with flash flooding of Arivaca Rd. in northwest Santa Cruz and southeast Pima counties.","162410":"A persistent rainy pattern across the southeastern big bend brought rainfall amounts in excess of foot during the first 12 days of the month to portions of southeastern Taylor, southern Lafayette, and Dixie counties. This rainfall fell on already saturated grounds and resulted in significant, long duration areal flooding. In addition, significant river flooding occurred across the Steinhatchee River basin. The Steinhatchee River crested at its 2nd highest crest on record at 24.6 ft on August 7th, which is well into the moderate flood category. Many roads were closed, and many homes were impacted. The river remained in at least minor flood stage for 20 days.","162620":"Despite weaker pre-storm deep-layer shear on the order of 25-30 knots and fairly narrow instability profiles of 1000-1500 J/kg, modifications on the storm scale and an increase in the low-level jet improved the environment enough to support several long-lived supercell clusters along a weak frontal boundary.","162638":"Despite weaker pre-storm deep-layer shear on the order of 25-30 knots and fairly narrow instability profiles of 1000-1500 J/kg, modifications on the storm scale and an increase in the low-level jet improved the environment enough to support several long-lived supercell clusters along a weak frontal boundary. Storms moving through the Sioux Falls area forced an early cancellation of the Sioux Empire Fair.","162644":"Weakening clusters of evening thunderstorms moved out of South Dakota and Minnesota into northwest Iowa.  A few storms produced hail and damaging wind.","162646":"A severe thunderstorm dropped one inch hail on the Munds Park area."},"events":[{"begin":"2021-08-06T00:12Z","county":"Park","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-08-06T00:12Z","endLat":46.16,"endLon":-110.38,"episode":161284,"id":973868,"injuries":0,"lat":46.16,"location":"15.66 ENE Wilsall Arpt","lon":-110.38,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","source":"Mesonet","state":"MT","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"BYZ"},{"begin":"2021-08-06T00:12Z","county":"Pipestone","deaths":0,"end":"2021-08-06T00:15Z","endLat":44.07,"endLon":-96.19,"episode":162620,"id":981889,"injuries":0,"lat":44.07,"location":"2.13 SSE Holland","lon":-96.19,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Corn flattened in a field around one and a half miles south of Holland. Several medium-sized branches also down in tree line.","source":"Public","state":"MN","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"FSD"},{"begin":"2021-08-06T00:15Z","county":"Moody","deaths":0,"end":"2021-08-06T00:17Z","endLat":44.11,"endLon":-96.83,"episode":162638,"id":981934,"injuries":0,"lat":44.11,"location":"9 N Colman","lon":-96.83,"magnitude":1.0,"source":"Trained Spotter","state":"SD","type":"Hail","wfo":"FSD"},{"begin":"2021-08-06T00:21Z","county":"Power","damageCrop